From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: alpha-liu-01 <116528196+alpha-liu-01@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 16:16:19 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] drm/msm/dsi: treat Xiaomi's ss-ea brightness flag as
 inverted DBV

Xiaomi's device trees mark panels that take the DCS brightness (DBV)
value big-endian with qcom,mdss-dsi-bl-dcs-type-ss-ea instead of the
upstream qcom,mdss-dsi-bl-inverted-dbv. Xiaomi's own kernel handles it;
this tree did not, so the m17 panel of the Redmi Note 12 5G got the bytes
swapped: most brightness levels were wrong, and the screen went black
when the lock screen set its first brightness. Accept the ss-ea flag as
inverted DBV.
---
 techpack/display/msm/dsi/dsi_panel.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/techpack/display/msm/dsi/dsi_panel.c b/techpack/display/msm/dsi/dsi_panel.c
index 698cc92b5..d95a7ab17 100644
--- a/techpack/display/msm/dsi/dsi_panel.c
+++ b/techpack/display/msm/dsi/dsi_panel.c
@@ -2479,8 +2479,11 @@ static int dsi_panel_parse_bl_config(struct dsi_panel *panel)
 		panel->bl_config.brightness_max_level = val;
 	}
 
+	/* Xiaomi DTs mark big-endian DCS brightness with ss-ea instead */
 	panel->bl_config.bl_inverted_dbv = utils->read_bool(utils->data,
-		"qcom,mdss-dsi-bl-inverted-dbv");
+		"qcom,mdss-dsi-bl-inverted-dbv") ||
+		utils->read_bool(utils->data,
+		"qcom,mdss-dsi-bl-dcs-type-ss-ea");
 
 	state = utils->get_property(utils->data, "qcom,bl-dsc-cmd-state", NULL);
 	if (!state || !strcmp(state, "dsi_hs_mode"))
